# Netlify. Defence in depth: even if a full template somehow ends up in the
# published directory, it is not reachable. The primary control is that
# scripts/build-site.mjs builds _site/ from an allowlist and hard-fails if a
# deliverable appears; this is the backstop.
#
# templates/assets/* must stay reachable — previews/ references it — so only the
# .html deliverables are blocked.

/templates/*.html   /404.html   404
/dist/*             /404.html   404
